.TH XEXPOSE 1 "2025-06-16" "xexpose 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xexpose \- lightweight window picker for X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xexpose
.RB [ \-a | \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-close ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xexpose
shows live thumbnails of all windows in a grid overlay, letting you
quickly switch between them. It works with any EWMH\-compliant X11
window manager.
.PP
Windows are displayed as scaled thumbnails with application icons and
titles. The current workspace is shown by default, with tabs at the
bottom for switching between workspaces.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show windows from all workspaces in a single grid. Windows on other
desktops that cannot provide composite pixmaps are shown as placeholders
with a centered application icon.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-close
Enable closing windows from the picker via middle\-click or the Delete key.
Disabled by default to prevent accidental closes.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS Keyboard
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Navigate between window thumbnails.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Cycle through windows (wraps around).
.TP
.B Enter
Activate the selected window.
.TP
.B Escape
Close the picker.
.TP
.BR PgUp ", " PgDn
Switch workspace.
.TP
.B Down (from bottom row)
Enter workspace tab navigation.
.TP
.B Super hold + Tab
Cycle windows; release Super to activate.
.TP
.B Type characters
Filter windows by title or WM class (case\-insensitive substring match).
.TP
.B Backspace
Remove the last filter character.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Backspace
Clear the filter.
.TP
.B Delete
Close the selected window (requires \fB\-\-allow\-close\fR).
.SS Mouse
.TP
.B Click
Activate the clicked window or switch workspace tab.
.TP
.B Middle\-click
Close the clicked window (requires \fB\-\-allow\-close\fR).
.TP
.B Hover
Highlight window or tab under the pointer.
.SH X RESOURCES
Appearance can be customized via X resources
.RB ( ~/.Xresources ).
The following resources are supported:
.TP
.B xexpose.foreground
Text color. Default: \fB#eeeeec\fR
.TP
.B xexpose.background
Background color for tabs, filter bar, and fallback when no wallpaper is set.
Default: \fB#2e3436\fR
.TP
.B xexpose.borderColor
Window thumbnail border and active tab color.
Default: \fB#555753\fR
.TP
.B xexpose.highlightColor
Selected window border and focused tab color.
Default: \fB#eeeeec\fR
.TP
.B xexpose.stickyColor
Border color for sticky (on\-all\-desktops) windows.
Default: \fB#edd400\fR
.TP
.B xexpose.font
Xft font name for titles and labels. Default: \fBsans\-10\fR.
.PP
Wildcard resources such as \fB*foreground\fR are also resolved through
Xrm's standard lookup rules.
.SH EXAMPLES
Bind to a key in marco:
.PP
.nf
gsettings set org.mate.Marco.keybinding\-commands command\-1 'xexpose'
gsettings set org.mate.Marco.global\-keybindings run\-command\-1 '<Super>Tab'
.fi
.PP
Show all workspaces with close enabled:
.PP
.nf
xexpose \-\-all \-\-allow\-close
.fi
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Xlib, XComposite (>= 0.3), XRender, Xfixes, Xft, Xinerama, Cairo.
